locks runs livespec (https://github.com/Rixmerz/livespec) as a separate
program and reads its index; it does not include livespec's code, which is
licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0.

locks includes skills written by others, each under its own license, kept in
src/locks/skills/ with its license file and the list of what locks changed
(src/locks/skills/README.md):

- from vise (https://github.com/Rixmerz/vise), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026
  Rixmerz: engineering-baseline, ponytail, security-baseline, architecture,
  ui-critique, web-ui-rules, design-brief and fourteen *-rules skills
  (src/locks/skills/LICENSE-vise);
- from Cloudflare's security-audit skill
  (https://github.com/cloudflare/security-audit-skill), MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Cloudflare, Inc.: security-audit
  (src/locks/skills/security-audit/LICENSE).

The roles in src/locks/roles/ adapt vise's agent charters (MIT, as above);
src/locks/roles/CREDITS.txt lists each one's sources.
